"""AQS-BLD-014 water tower (Q-009 closed by the owner 2026-10-16): the top floors are the pumped-hydro upper reservoir, CATCH_TANK the lower.
Solver flow_graph/param/water_tower.py (A-M-187). Also rewrites the placement datums so the roof PV sits on the reservoir roof and L-2 at
the lower-reservoir floor. Run: python3 docs-authority/_water_tower.py"""
import json, os, sys
R = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(R); sys.path.insert(0, R); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(R, 'models/freecad'))
import params as P
from flow_graph.param import water_tower as WT
from flow_graph.param.refs import cite
r = P.HYDRO; s = WT.seismic_wind(r, P.PLATE_L, P.PLATE_W); d = json.load(open('flow_graph/param/drivers.json')); v = lambda k: d[k]['value']
sp = 'flow_graph/placement_seed.json'; S = json.load(open(sp)); D = S['datums_mm']; old = dict(D)
D['L-2'] = P.Z_Lm2; D['ROOF'] = P.Z_ROOF
for i in range(r['levels']): D[f'R{i+1}'] = P.HYDRO_RES_Z0 + i*P.HYDRO_RES_CLEAR
for u in S['units']:
    if u.get('level') in ('ROOF', 'L-2') and u.get('origin_mm'): u['origin_mm'][2] = D[u['level']] + (P.SLAB_THK if u['level'] == 'L-2' else 0)
for u in S['units']:
    if u['unit_id'] == 'CATCH_TANK': u['size_mm'] = [P.CATCH_TANK_L, P.CATCH_TANK_W, P.CATCH_TANK_H]; u['origin_mm'] = [P.CATCH_TANK_X, P.CATCH_TANK_Y, P.CATCH_TANK_Z]
json.dump(S, open(sp, 'w'), indent=2)
c = [cite(k) for k in ('ASCE7_22', 'ACI350_3', 'ACI350_20', 'IBC2027_CH10', 'NFPA101_2027', 'DOE_PSH')]
kN = r['water_t']*9.81; A = r['area_m2']
md = ['# Water tower: pumped-hydro reservoirs in the building', '', 'Document number: AQS-BLD-014', 'Revision: A', 'Date: 2026-10-16',
 'Authority: AQS-PLAN-007 X-RED-02; owner decision Q-009 (closed 2026-10-16): build the top floors as the upper reservoir. Generated by `docs-authority/_water_tower.py` from `flow_graph/param/water_tower.py`. Study. A-M-187.', '',
 '## Sizing from need', '',
 f"Store: {r['E_kWh']:.1f} kWh at the bus (HYDRO_SET backup basis, NFPA 111 Class X, A-M-145). Turbine-generator {v('hydro_eta_turbine')} (DOE_PSH) less {v('wt_penstock_loss_frac')*100:.0f} % penstock friction gives {r['eta_net']:.2f}.",
 f"Head is the drop between the water centroids, upper full to lower full. It depends on the reservoir depth, so the solver iterates: V = E / (rho g h eta).", '',
 '| Item | Value |', '|---|---|',
 f"| Head (centroid to centroid) | {r['head_m']:.2f} m |", f"| Water | {r['V_m3']:.0f} m3 live + {r['V_fire_m3']:.0f} m3 fire reserve below the hydro outlet (AQS-SAF-005) = {r['water_t']:.0f} t |",
 f"| Reservoir plan area (plate less {v('wt_core_frac')*100:.0f} % cores) | {A:.0f} m2 |",
 f"| Upper reservoir | {r['levels']} levels at {r['level_clear_m']:.1f} m floor-to-floor above the ROOF_TANK storey, {r['depth_per_level_m']:.2f} m water each (max {v('wt_water_max_m')} m), {r['cells_per_level']} cells per level of {r['cell_len_m']:.1f} m |",
 f"| Upper reservoir floor / roof | +{r['z_res0_m']:.1f} m / +{r['z_roof_m']:.1f} m |",
 f"| Lower reservoir (CATCH_TANK) | {r['catch_depth_m']:.2f} m water + {v('wt_freeboard_m')} m freeboard over {A:.0f} m2, floor at {r['z_catch_floor_m']:.2f} m |",
 f"| Penstock static pressure | {1000*9.81*(r['z_res0_m'] - r['z_catch_floor_m'])/1e6:.2f} MPa at the turbine |", '',
 f"Each reservoir level is split into at least two cells, each with its own outlet valve to the penstock, so one cell can be drained for inspection while the store keeps {100*(r['cells_per_level']*r['levels'] - 1)/(r['cells_per_level']*r['levels']):.0f} % of its energy (redundancy rule).", '',
 'Building rule (owner): as the plant grows, HAB/FARM levels are added at ' + f"{v('wt_life_per_shop')} x the rate of shop levels (LIFE_LEVELS = 1 + {v('wt_life_per_shop')} (SHOP_LEVELS - 1)). A taller life stack raises the head and the reservoir shrinks in step. At this scale: {P.SHOP_LEVELS} shop, {P.LIFE_LEVELS} life level(s).", '',
 '## CATCH_TANK basis (check)', '',
 'The earlier CATCH_TANK was a fixed 12 x 8 x 4 m box scaled by plate area (384 m3; 3,916 kN test load in AQS-BLD-013 rev A). That was not from need. It is now the lower reservoir and holds the full upper volume plus freeboard; terrace rain catch uses the freeboard and overflows to the site drain. The tank is ' + f"{P.CATCH_TANK_L/1000:.1f} x {P.CATCH_TANK_W/1000:.1f} x {P.CATCH_TANK_H/1000:.2f} m.", '',
 '## Structural loads (ASCE7_22, ACI350_3, ACI350_20)', '',
 '| Load | Value | Basis |', '|---|---|---|',
 f"| Water weight, upper | {kN:.0f} kN ({kN/r['levels']/A:.1f} kPa per reservoir slab) | operating = test (full) |",
 f"| Seismic base shear from the water mass | {s['V_seis_kN']:.0f} kN (Cs {s['Cs']:.2f}) | ASCE 7 12.8, SDS {v('wt_SDS')}, R {v('wt_R')}, Ie {v('wt_Ie')} (Risk Cat. IV), impulsive mass taken rigid |",
 f"| Seismic overturning at grade | {s['M_seis_kNm']:.0f} kN m | water centroid height |",
 f"| Convective period, sloshing height | {s['Tc_s']:.2f} s, {s['slosh_m']:.2f} m (Sac {s['Sac']:.3f} g) | ACI 350.3 rectangular cell, ASCE 7 15.7.6.1.2 |",
 f"| Freeboard in each reservoir level | {r['level_clear_m'] - 0.3 - r['depth_per_level_m']:.2f} m, {'covers' if s['freeboard_ok'] else 'DOES NOT cover'} the sloshing height | soffit must not take wave impact |",
 f"| Wind on the reservoir storeys | {s['F_wind_kN']:.0f} kN (qz {s['qz_kPa']:.2f} kPa at {s['H_roof_m']:.1f} m) | ASCE 7 ch. 26-27, exposure C, {v('wt_wind_ms')} m/s |", '',
 f"Seismic governs over wind by {s['V_seis_kN']/s['F_wind_kN']:.0f} x. The lateral system (X-BLD-01) and the foundations (X-BLD-03) must carry it; walls and slabs that retain water follow ACI 350 crack control. Site SDS, SD1 and wind speed are assumptions until the geotechnical report (A-M-187).", '',
 '## Egress and access (IBC2027_CH10, NFPA101_2027)', '',
 'The reservoir levels are unoccupied: maintenance access only. The two exit stairs (IBC 1006.3.3) continue through the reservoir storeys to the roof for PV service (IBC 1011.12), in the core fraction above. Each cell has a hatch, ladder and confined-space entry procedure. The reservoir floors add no occupant load and no travel distance to the life floors.', '',
 '## Roof PV', '',
 f"The PV array moves to the reservoir roof at +{r['z_roof_m']:.1f} m (datum ROOF). The footprint is unchanged, so the roof area and the PV area (solver.roof_close) are unchanged; the PV dead load now lands on the reservoir roof slab.", '',
 f"Placement datums changed: L-2 {old.get('L-2')} -> {D['L-2']} mm, ROOF {old.get('ROOF')} -> {D['ROOF']} mm, added " + ', '.join(f"R{i+1} {D[f'R{i+1}']}" for i in range(r['levels'])) + ' mm.']
open('docs-authority/WATER_TOWER.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md) + '\n'); print(r['levels'], round(r['head_m'], 2), round(r['V_m3']))
